configuration:ABoxFileConvention a configuration:NamingConvention,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ABox File Naming Convention"@en ;
    configuration:appliesToArtifactType configuration:ABoxFile ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "{prefix}_abox_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "Parallels ShapeFileConvention's {prefix}_shacl_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl pattern. The 'abox' type qualifier prevents silent overwrite when copied alongside the TBox or combined ontology file."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Applies when an ontology is split into terminology + instances. The combined form (using OntologyFileConvention) remains the default; ABoxFileConvention is used only when the split is intentional. The ABox file SHOULD declare owl:imports of its companion TBox file."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-4-tbox-abox-extension> ;
    skos:definition "The mandatory filename pattern for ABox-only ontology files (configuration:ABoxFile): {prefix}_abox_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl, where {prefix} is the short name of the ontology subject, 'abox' is a fixed type qualifier, and v{M}_{m}_{p} encodes the file's own version. RULED 2026-07-28 (Phase D, a registrant package proposal): this convention also governs governance-register data files (an adopting development's backlog/roadmap/evidence instances). No new convention or exception individual is minted for this case, per L-110 restraint on minting governance structure on a single producer’s evidence (catalogued at v20.24.0; this clause as first written cited a different best practice that does not state the principle — the citation is corrected here, the ruling itself is unchanged): the filename pattern is followed exactly. The one real divergence — such a file versions per working-session verification rather than per pack release — is recorded here as a fact about usage, not a filename exception, since no delimiter or pattern deviation exists to except (unlike SafeguardDotDelimiterException/USODelimiterException, which are VersionInFilenamePolicy exceptions for genuine format divergence). A consumer needing to distinguish a live register from a released ABox should read backlog:RegisterSession, not the filename."@en ;
    skos:example """meta_abox_v6_7_1.ttl — prefix='meta', M=6, m=7, p=1 ✓
oqc_abox_v2_3_2.ttl ✓
amod_abox_v1_5.ttl — VIOLATION: missing patch token"""@en .

