configuration:ProjectArchiveCapitalisedException a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project Archive Capitalised Exception"@en ;
    configuration:appliesToArtifactType configuration:ProjectArchive ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "Oepack_{Scope}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.zip"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "Real-corpus observation: Oepack_phase1_v1_0_0.zip, Oepack_phase2_.zip, Oepack_phase3_v1_0_0.zip uploaded by parallel-session author."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This variant aligns with the v1.4.0 ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention case style ('Sprint_8_Closure_v1_0_0.md'), so it has internal logic — but it diverges from established Unix/web filename conventions. Documented for completeness and grandfathering, not endorsed for new archives."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-1-archive-extension> ;
    skos:definition "ACCEPTED HISTORICAL VARIANT: project-archive filenames using capitalised 'Oepack' prefix and underscore separators throughout (matching ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention's case style). Regex: ^Oepack_[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.zip$. Observed in parallel-session uploads (Oepack_phase1_v1_0_0.zip family). NEW archives SHOULD use the canonical lowercase-hyphen form (configuration:ProjectArchiveConvention); this variant is acceptable for archives produced by tooling that follows the markdown filename style end-to-end."@en .

configuration:ProjectArchiveConvention a configuration:NamingConvention,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project archive convention"@en ;
    configuration:appliesToArtifactType configuration:ProjectArchive ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "oepack-{scope}-v{M}_{m}_{p}.zip"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack family handoff archive (oepack-newsession-handoff-v1_0_0.zip) — the cleanest existing precedent."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Why hyphen for scope but underscore for version: hyphen is standard for filename word separators (per RFC 3986 — also URL-safe and shell-friendly), while underscore-3-part-version preserves alignment with the 3-part SemVer pattern used in OntologyFileConvention and ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention. Mixing the two is INTENTIONAL — same precedent as USOVocabularyModuleConvention (hyphen for scope, underscore for version)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-1-archive-extension> ;
    skos:definition "Enforces the canonical OE Pack project-archive filename pattern: lowercase 'oepack' prefix, hyphen-delimited multi-segment scope, hyphenated 'v' marker, underscore-delimited 3-part SemVer, .zip extension. Regex: ^oepack-[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*-v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.zip$. Rationale: hyphenated scope echoes USOVocabularyModuleConvention (which uses 'uso-{module}-v{M}_{m}.ttl'); 3-part underscore version echoes ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention (v1.4.0). Combines two existing AMOD precedents into a single coherent zip pattern."@en ;
    skos:example """oepack-newsession-handoff-v1_0_0.zip ✅
oepack-phase1-v1_0_0.zip ✅ (canonical)
oepack-parallel-integration-v1_0_1.zip ✅ (canonical)
oepack-sprint8-deliverables-v2_3_0.zip ✅ (canonical — multi-word scope OK)"""@en .

configuration:ProjectArchiveDotVersionException a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project Archive DOT-version Exception"@en ;
    configuration:appliesToArtifactType configuration:ProjectArchive ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "oepack-{scope}-v{M}.{m}.{p}.zip"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "Real-corpus observation: oepack-phase1-v1.0.0.zip, oepack-phase2-v1.0.0.zip, oepack-phase3-v1.0.0.zip shipped under this form."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Documented as a separate individual rather than a regex alternative because the rationale differs: SafeguardDocConvention uses dot intentionally to differentiate from OntologyFile; ProjectArchiveDotVersion is just legacy filename style that wasn't governed before this extension. Marking it as accepted-but-not-canonical."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-1-archive-extension> ;
    skos:definition "ACCEPTED HISTORICAL VARIANT: project-archive filenames using DOT-delimited 3-part version (v1.0.0) instead of underscore (v1_0_0). Regex: ^oepack-[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*-v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\\.zip$. Observed in oepack-phase1-v1.0.0.zip and family. NEW archives SHOULD use the canonical underscore form (configuration:ProjectArchiveConvention); the DOT form is grandfathered for existing archives but not preferred for new ones. Difference from configuration:SafeguardDotDelimiterException: that one is for .md SafeguardDocuments and uses 2-part version; this one is for .zip ProjectArchives and uses 3-part."@en .

configuration:ProjectArchiveVsMarkdownException a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project Archive vs Project Markdown convention exception"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "AMOD v1.4.1 design rationale; parallel structure to v1.4.0 configuration:ProjectMarkdownVsSafeguardException."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Without this exception declared, a reader might wonder 'why does v1.4.0 use Capitalised_Names but v1.4.1 uses lowercase-names'? The reason is artefact-type-specific: archives are filesystem objects, markdown is human-readable text. v1.4.1 follows the Unix/web convention for binary distribution artefacts (matching USO module precedent), while v1.4.0 follows the IDE/human-reading convention for text documents."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-1-archive-extension> ;
    skos:definition "INTENTIONAL DUAL-CONVENTION: configuration:ProjectArchive (zip files) and configuration:ProjectMarkdownDocument (md files) are different artefact types with different filename conventions even though both are project-level deliverables. Archive convention: lowercase 'oepack' prefix + hyphen-delimited scope + underscore-3-part-version + .zip. Markdown convention: capitalised name + underscore-delimited words + underscore-3-part-version + .md. The case difference (lowercase oepack vs capitalised) reflects file-system vs human-document conventions: archives are accessed via shell/scripts (lowercase + hyphen friendly), markdown documents are read by humans in IDEs (capitalised reads as a title). Neither convention overrides the other; AMOD S6+ shapes apply each convention only to its declared subclass."@en .

configuration:ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention a configuration:NamingConvention,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project Closure Markdown Naming Convention"@en,
        "Project closure markdown convention"@en ;
    configuration:appliesToArtifactType configuration:ProjectClosureDocument,
        configuration:ProjectClosureMarkdown ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "{Capitalised_name}_Closure_v{M}_{m}_{p}.md",
        "{name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.md"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "Issue I-04 closure (Phase 1)."@en,
        "OE Pack family Sprint 0-8 actually-shipped closure documents (Sprint_0_Closure_v1_0_0.md … Sprint_8_Closure_v1_0_0.md)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Why this exists: AMOD v1.2.6 ships SafeguardDocConvention with pattern '{prefix}_safeguard_{variant}_v{M}.{m}.md' (DOT delimiter, 2-part version). User house style for closure docs uses underscore + 3-part SemVer. Without this convention, every closure document Sprint 0-8 ships triggers an AMOD S6 violation. ProjectClosureMarkdownConvention closes the gap with a parallel pattern that matches actual practice."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration>,
        <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-0-naming-extension> ;
    skos:definition "Enforces the actually-shipped pattern for OE Pack closure markdown documents: capitalised name component, underscore-as-separator, three-part SemVer, capitalised 'Closure' marker, .md extension. Regex: ^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(_[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*)*_Closure_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.md$. PARALLEL to configuration:SafeguardDocConvention — does NOT replace it. Different artefact type, different convention."@en,
        "Filename pattern for ProjectClosureDocument: underscore-delimited 3-part version. Distinct from SafeguardDocConvention (DOT, 2-part) and DocumentationFileConvention (underscore, 2-part)."@en ;
    skos:example """Sprint_8_Closure_v1_0_0.md  ✓
Implementation_Plan_v1_0_0.md  ✓
STEP_0_I17_Closure_v1_0_0.md  ✓
my_doc_v1_0.md  ✗ (use DocumentationFileConvention)"""@en,
        "Sprint_8_Closure_v1_0_0.md ✅ ; ReviewSprint_Closure_v1_0_0.md ✅ ; Phase1_Closure_v1_0_0.md ✅ ; sprint8_closure_v1.0.md ❌ (lowercase + dot — would match SafeguardDocConvention if filename ended with _safeguard_)."@en .

configuration:ProjectMarkdownVsSafeguardException a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Project markdown vs SafeguardDocument convention exception"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "AMOD v1.4.0 design rationale; OE Pack Issue I-04."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Without this exception declared, a reader of AMOD might wonder 'doesn't AMOD already have a markdown convention via SafeguardDocConvention?' — Yes, but ONLY for SafeguardDocument. ProjectMarkdownDocument is a different type that didn't exist in v1.2.6. AMOD v1.4.0 fills the gap rather than redefining the existing pattern."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration-v1-4-0-naming-extension> ;
    skos:definition "INTENTIONAL DUAL-CONVENTION: configuration:SafeguardDocument and configuration:ProjectMarkdownDocument are different artefact types with different filename conventions. SafeguardDocument uses '{prefix}_safeguard_{variant}_v{M}.{m}.md' (DOT, 2-part, lowercase). ProjectMarkdownDocument subclasses (ProjectClosureMarkdown, PlanMarkdown, AuditReportMarkdown) use 3-part SemVer with underscore delimiter. The two conventions are parallel — neither overrides the other. AMOD S6 SHACL shape correctly applies SafeguardDocConvention only to configuration:SafeguardDocument instances; the new project-markdown conventions apply only to their subclasses. No conflict, no override."@en .

configuration:REDOEcosystemSchema a configuration:ArtifactNamingSchema,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "a reliability ontology Ontology Engineering Ecosystem Naming Schema"@en ;
    configuration:filenamePattern "COLLECTION: {prefix}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl | {prefix}_shacl_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl | {prefix}_safeguard_{variant}_v{M}.{m}.md | {name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.html | {name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.{ext}" ;
    configuration:hasNamingConvention configuration:CodeModuleConvention,
        configuration:HtmlArtifactConvention,
        configuration:OntologyFileConvention,
        configuration:SafeguardDocConvention,
        configuration:ShapeFileConvention ;
    configuration:includesConvention configuration:CodeModuleConvention,
        configuration:DocumentationFileConvention,
        configuration:HtmlArtifactConvention,
        configuration:OntologyFileConvention,
        configuration:SafeguardDocConvention,
        configuration:ShapeFileConvention ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "a reliability ontology ecosystem sprint engineering practice, April 2026. USO v2.0 Sprint 12 post-mortem. ISO/IEC 15289:2019 Systems and software engineering — Content of life-cycle information items."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Singleton — one schema per project. Referenced by redo:hasManifest from redo:C8Out instances to provide the naming validation context for sprint closure."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    skos:definition "The project-level ArtifactNamingSchema for the a reliability ontology ontology engineering ecosystem, collecting the five NamingConvention instances that govern all artefact types produced in the ecosystem: OntologyFileConvention, ShapeFileConvention, SafeguardDocConvention, HtmlArtifactConvention, and CodeModuleConvention. This schema is the authoritative reference consulted by the a reliability ontology C8Out gate when validating sprint manifest entries."@en ;
    skos:example "Applies to all a reliability ontology ecosystem outputs: redo_v2_*.ttl, redo_shacl_v*.ttl, redo_safeguard_*_v*.md, *_v*.html, *_v*.jsx"@en .

