measurement:Tier_B_StatisticalProxy a measurement:ConfidenceTier,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TIER-B: Statistical Proxy"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v19.6.0 Phase J1 / BP-D47."@en ;
    skos:definition "TIER-B confidence tier: scores produced by static computation using statistical/heuristic models that proxy for runtime or external properties. Reproducible across runs but the interpretation is probabilistic. Examples: OQuaRE Availability via LCOMOnto (Duque-Ramos 2016 Table 3 published proxy), reasoning-time band prediction from class count + axiom density, defect-proneness ranking from coupling metrics, OQuaRE dynamic scaling percentile bands. Aggregations containing any TIER-B score (and no TIER-C or TIER-D) are TIER-B."@en .

measurement:Tier_C_LLMMediated a measurement:ConfidenceTier,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TIER-C: LLM-Mediated"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v19.6.0 Phase J1 / BP-D47."@en ;
    skos:definition "TIER-C confidence tier: scores produced by querying a Large Language Model for semantic judgment. Not bit-reproducible across LLM runs even at temperature=0 (cache-level reproducibility achievable via prompt-version-locked caching). Inherits the model's training-time biases. Examples: OOPS P05/P14/P15/P16/P17/P18 semantic-correctness pitfalls judged by LLM, FAIR R1.3 community-standards conformance, naming-quality judgment beyond regex. Aggregations containing any TIER-C score are TIER-C."@en .

measurement:Tier_D_HumanJudgment a measurement:ConfidenceTier,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TIER-D: Human Judgment"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    skos:definition "TIER-D confidence tier: scores produced by a human expert's semantic judgment. Not bit-reproducible across assessors, but accountable and open to review; distinct from Tier_C (LLM-mediated). Order of confidence A, B, D, C: aggregations containing any TIER-D score (and no TIER-C) are TIER-D."@en .

