ns3:ArithmeticMeanRule_v1 a quality:ArithmeticMeanRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Arithmetic mean rule (v1 scoring)"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "score_ontologies.py v1; ISO/IEC 25023:2016 §7.1."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Strictly weaker than WeightedSumRule when dimensions have different importance — captured here as a NamedIndividual so reproducibility audits can identify which scoring rule was used for any given QualityAssessment."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "The unweighted arithmetic-mean aggregation used in v1 of the OE Pack scoring scripts. Computes composite = (Σ scores) / |scores| over all dimensions equally. Produces values around 0.74 on the v15.4 stack — the lower of the two reference numbers cited in PR1 §3.1. Captures v1 methodology so it can be queried, audited, or rerun without referencing the implementation script directly."@en ;
    skos:example "Composite for an ontology with InheritanceRichness=0.85, ClassRichness=0.62, AttributeRichness=0.71, RelationshipRichness=0.59: (0.85+0.62+0.71+0.59)/4 = 0.6925."@en .

ns3:CQ1_AvailableRules a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Which aggregation rules can a QualityAssessment reference?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?rule WHERE { { ?rule rdf:type quality:WeightedSumRule } UNION { ?rule rdf:type quality:ArithmeticMeanRule } UNION { ?rule rdf:type quality:OQuaRETierWeightedRule } }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Aggregation Rules v1.0.0 §1."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by SPARQL: SELECT ?r WHERE { ?r a qc:AggregationRule } UNION { ?r a/rdfs:subClassOf+ qc:AggregationRule }. Returns ArithmeticMeanRule_v1, WeightedSum_QCore70_Structural30_v2, OQuaRETierWeighted_default, GeometricMean_balanced."@en .

ns3:CQ2_RuleWeightLookup a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "What weights does a given WeightedSum rule use?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?rule ?qcore ?struct WHERE { ?rule rdf:type quality:WeightedSumRule ; oem:weightQCore ?qcore ; oem:weightStructural ?struct }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Aggregation Rules v1.0.0 §2."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by SPARQL: SELECT ?wq ?ws WHERE { ?rule :weightQCore ?wq ; :weightStructural ?ws }. Returns 0.7/0.3 for the v2 rule and OQuaRE default."@en .

ns3:CQ3_RuleProvenance a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Which scoring script implements which aggregation rule?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?rule ?source WHERE { { ?rule rdf:type quality:WeightedSumRule } UNION { ?rule rdf:type quality:ArithmeticMeanRule } UNION { ?rule rdf:type quality:OQuaRETierWeightedRule } OPTIONAL { ?rule dcterms:source ?source } }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Aggregation Rules v1.0.0 — dcterms:source on each rule."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by SPARQL: SELECT ?rule ?source WHERE { ?rule a/rdfs:subClassOf* qc:AggregationRule ; dcterms:source ?source }. Each rule cites its source paper plus the implementation script (score_ontologies.py for v1, score_ontologies_v2.py for v2 + OQuaRE)."@en .

ns3:GeometricMean_balanced a measurement:GeometricMeanRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Geometric mean rule (balanced — penalises any low score)"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "ISO/IEC 25023:2016 §7.3."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Provided as a contrast to ArithmeticMeanRule_v1 to make the rule space explicit. Adoption is a methodology choice — not currently the default."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "Alternative aggregation where composite = (Π scores)^(1/n). Penalises any single low score more aggressively than arithmetic or weighted-sum rules — useful when no quality dimension should be neglected. Currently NOT used by any production scoring script in the OE Pack ecosystem; included here for completeness so future assessments that need 'no-low-dimension' semantics can reference it."@en ;
    skos:example "v1-style scores 0.85, 0.62, 0.71, 0.59 → arithmetic mean = 0.69, geometric mean = (0.85×0.62×0.71×0.59)^(1/4) = 0.687. Difference grows when any score approaches 0."@en .

ns3:OQuaRETierWeighted_default a quality:OQuaRETierWeightedRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OQuaRE tier-weighted rule (default — Duque-Ramos 2011 §3.5)"@en ;
    measurement:weightQCore 0.7 ;
    measurement:weightStructural 0.3 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "Duque-Ramos et al. (2011) §3.5 'OQuaRE composite quality measure'; OQC v2.3.0 §Aggregation extension."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This is the rule referenced by Score_OE_v15_4_Weighted_StackMean in the existing oqc_measurements_v15_4 ABox demo. Without this NamedIndividual, that score's source rule was structurally unattributable. v1.0.0 of THIS file makes the link queryable."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "The canonical OQuaRE composite as published. Specialises the v2 70/30 weighted sum by adding role-aware threshold bands (foundation / meta / domain / application) — different ontology roles get different OQuaRE 1-5 thresholds for the same metric, reflecting that an InheritanceRichness of 0.3 is excellent for a foundation ontology and mediocre for a domain ontology. The default 0.7/0.3 weights match v2's; what's distinctive is the role-aware band computation."@en ;
    skos:example "InheritanceRichness=0.85 on a foundation ontology → 5/5 (within 0.2..0.7 band per qc:TR_NOMInh_foundation_5). Same metric on a domain ontology → 3/5 (0.5..1.5 acceptable but not optimal)."@en .

ns3:WeightedSum_QCore70_Structural30_v2 a quality:WeightedSumRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Weighted sum rule — Q-Core 0.7 / Structural 0.3 (v2 scoring)"@en ;
    measurement:weightQCore 0.7 ;
    measurement:weightStructural 0.3 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "score_ontologies_v2.py; ISO/IEC 25023:2016 §7.2; PR1 §3.1 reference numbers."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Weight choice rationale: PR1 §3.3 — 'Q-Core captures defects that should never be present; Structural captures growth dimensions that vary by ontology purpose. Q-Core dominates because no defect-free ontology should be penalised for structural variation.' If a future audit wants to challenge this rationale, instantiate an alternative WeightedSumRule with different weights and compare."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-aggregation-rules> ;
    skos:definition "The 70/30 weighted-sum rule used in v2 of the OE Pack scoring scripts. Composite = 0.7 × (Q-Core composite) + 0.3 × (Structural composite). Q-Core captures binary defect dimensions (HermiT consistency, validation pass-rate, PROV completeness); Structural captures OQuaRE 1-5 ranges (InheritanceRichness, ClassRichness, etc.). Produces the 0.98 stack mean cited in PR1 §3.1 — the higher of the two reference numbers. Differs from the parent qc:WeightedSumRule class by committing to specific weight values."@en ;
    skos:example "Stack assessment: Q-Core composite 1.00 + Structural composite 0.95 → weighted = 0.7×1.00 + 0.3×0.95 = 0.985. Matches Score_OE_v15_4_Weighted_StackMean = 0.9841 in oqc_measurements_v15_4 (ABox demo)."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage#CQ1_LinkedFormulas> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Which metrics have SPARQL implementations linked?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?metric ?formula WHERE { ?metric quality:hasSPARQLImplementation ?formula }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Formula Linkage Patch v1.0.0."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by SPARQL: SELECT ?metric ?impl WHERE { ?metric a/rdfs:subClassOf* qc:Metric . ?ind a ?metric . ?ind qc:hasSPARQLImplementation ?impl }. Returns 32 rows after this patch is loaded."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage#CQ2_FormulaForMetric> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "What is the SPARQL formula for InheritanceRichness?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?formula WHERE { ?m quality:hasSPARQLImplementation ?formula . FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?m), \"InheritanceRichness\")) }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Formula Linkage Patch v1.0.0."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by: SELECT ?q WHERE { ?ind a qc:InheritanceRichness ; qc:hasSPARQLImplementation ?q }. Returns the SPARQL query string from oqc_v2_3_1_sparql_impl line 73 area."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage#CQ3_FormulaCount> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "How many metric subclasses have implementations?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?metric) AS ?n) WHERE { ?metric quality:hasSPARQLImplementation ?f }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/quality> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Formula Linkage Patch v1.0.0."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-formula-linkage> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by: SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?metric) AS ?n) WHERE { ?metric rdfs:subClassOf*/rdfs:subClassOf* qc:Metric . ?ind a ?metric ; qc:hasSPARQLImplementation ?q }. Returns 32."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements#Assessment_OE_v15_4> a quality:QualityAssessment,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OE Pack v15.4 Stack Quality Assessment"@en ;
    quality:appliesAggregationRule <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#AggRule_OE_v15_4> ;
    quality:assessesArtifact <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#AMOD_v1_2_6>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#CORE_v1_1_7>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#META_v6_3_13>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#OQC_v2_2_5>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#REDO_v2_5_16> ;
    quality:atTimestamp "2026-05-04T22:26:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    quality:hasMetric <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#M_StackMean_QCore>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#M_StackMean_Structural>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#M_StackMean_Weighted> ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "score_v15_4.py + scores_v15_4.json + this ABox file."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements> ;
    prov:atTime "2026-05-04T22:26:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:generated <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#Score_OE_v15_4_QCore_StackMean>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#Score_OE_v15_4_Structural_StackMean>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#Score_OE_v15_4_Weighted_StackMean> .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements#OQuaRE_DefaultThresholds_2026> a measurement:ThresholdTable,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OQuaRE Default Thresholds (2026 baseline)"@en ;
    measurement:hasThresholdRow <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_CR_domain_3>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_CR_domain_4>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_CR_domain_5>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_CR_foundation_5>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_NOMInh_domain_5>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_NOMInh_foundation_5>,
        <http://example.org/oqc-measurements#TR_NOMInh_meta_5> ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "Duque-Ramos et al. (2011) §3.4 OQuaRE Table 4, with role-aware adaptations encoded in score_v15_4.py oquare_score()."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The threshold table currently used by the v15.4 scoring engine. Each row covers (metric, role, range, score)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements> ;
    skos:definition "The threshold table currently used by the v15.4 scoring engine. Each row covers (metric, role, range, score). (Originally a rdfs:comment; promoted to skos:definition in Sprint F2 per L-47v2 path (a) — the measurement:Measurement target class's shape requires skos:definition with minCount=1.)"@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements#ScoreEngine_v15_4> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "score_v15_4.py"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "/mnt/user-data/outputs/score_v15_4.py SHA-256 bc852fb03e49b33f1268f057c42de57288685ed207ffcaaf70eb41584def34f7."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements> .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-shapes#CQ1_ShapeCoverage> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Which OQC measurement classes have SHACL shapes?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT DISTINCT ?cls WHERE { ?cls rdf:type owl:Class . ?shape sh:targetClass ?cls . FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?cls), \"http://example.org/measurement#\")) }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Measurement Shapes v1.0.0 §1-4."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements-shapes> ;
    skos:definition "Resolved by SPARQL: SELECT ?cls WHERE { ?shape sh:targetClass ?cls } over this file. Returns qc:QualityAssessment, qc:Score, qc:ThresholdRow, qc:AggregationRule."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-shapes#CQ2_AssessmentRequirements> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "What does a valid QualityAssessment require?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?shape ?path WHERE { ?shape sh:targetClass quality:QualityAssessment ; sh:property ?prop . ?prop sh:path ?path }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OQC Measurement Shapes v1.0.0 §1."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements-shapes> ;
    skos:definition "Per :QualityAssessmentShape: ≥1 qc:assessesArtifact, exactly 1 qc:appliesAggregationRule, ≥1 qc:hasScore, optional 1 qc:atTimestamp. Violations are sh:Violation; missing timestamp is sh:Warning."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/Score_oee_v3_0_0_OEE_AlignmentDocumentationCompleteness> a measurement:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OEE v3.0.0 — Alignment Documentation Completeness Score"@en ;
    measurement:derivedFromMetric quality:I_OEE_AlignmentDocumentationCompleteness ;
    measurement:hasConfidenceTier measurement:Tier_A_StaticAlgorithmic ;
    quality:value 1.0 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack Phase 2.3 — measured value. Normalization: Already in [0,1]. Raw measurement value: 1.0. Normalized to [0,1]: 1.0."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/> ;
    skos:definition "Measurement score: OEE v3.0.0 — Alignment Documentation Completeness Score. Per Sprint F1 (Track A4 type-redirect from quality:Score → measurement:Score), oe-measurement SHACL requires skos:definition on Score individuals."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/Score_oee_v3_0_0_OEE_AlignmentRationaleCount> a measurement:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OEE v3.0.0 — Alignment Rationale Instance Count Score"@en ;
    measurement:derivedFromMetric quality:I_OEE_AlignmentRationaleCount ;
    measurement:hasConfidenceTier measurement:Tier_A_StaticAlgorithmic ;
    quality:value 0.2 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack Phase 2.3 — measured value. Normalization: Raw count / 5 (target rationale density for mature alignment ontology). Raw measurement value: 1. Normalized to [0,1]: 0.2."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/> ;
    skos:definition "Measurement score: OEE v3.0.0 — Alignment Rationale Instance Count Score. Per Sprint F1 (Track A4 type-redirect from quality:Score → measurement:Score), oe-measurement SHACL requires skos:definition on Score individuals."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/Score_oee_v3_0_0_OEE_CQCount> a measurement:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OEE v3.0.0 — Competency Question Count Score"@en ;
    measurement:derivedFromMetric quality:I_OEE_CQCount ;
    measurement:hasConfidenceTier measurement:Tier_A_StaticAlgorithmic ;
    quality:value 0.3 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/measurement> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack Phase 2.3 — measured value. Normalization: Raw count / 10 (target density for focused alignment ontology). Raw measurement value: 3. Normalized to [0,1]: 0.3."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/> ;
    skos:definition "Measurement score: OEE v3.0.0 — Competency Question Count Score. Per Sprint F1 (Track A4 type-redirect from quality:Score → measurement:Score), oe-measurement SHACL requires skos:definition on Score individuals."@en .

<http://example.org/oqc-measurements-v17/Score_oee_v3_0_0_OEE_CQResolutionCompleteness> a measurement:Score,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
