<http://example.org/redo-c7-split#CQ1_StrictVsAdvisoryDistinction> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "When does C7+ Strict fire vs. C7+ Advisory?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation "SELECT ?shape ?sev ?lbl WHERE { ?shape rdf:type sh:NodeShape ; rdfs:label ?lbl . FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?lbl), \"C7+\")) OPTIONAL { ?shape sh:severity ?sev } }"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "a reliability ontology C7+ split v1.0.0 §1-2."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/redo-c7-split> ;
    skos:definition "Strict (Violation) fires when rdf:type is from no known namespace — likely a typo or undeclared class. Advisory (Warning) fires when rdf:type IS from a known OE Pack namespace but not declared in the current data graph — likely a standalone-validation artefact, fixable by re-validating with imports merged."@en .

<http://example.org/redo-c7-split#CQ2_NamespaceWhitelist> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        core:OperationalizableCompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Which namespaces does C7+ Strict accept without inspection?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation """PREFIX sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX reliability: <http://example.org/reliability#>
# Returns the SPARQL FILTER body of the C7+ Strict shape, which embeds the allowlist
SELECT ?shape ?sparqlBody WHERE {
  ?shape a sh:NodeShape ;
         sh:sparql ?sb .
  ?sb sh:select ?sparqlBody .
  FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?shape), "C7plus_strict"))
}"""^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v17.30.0 — operationalized via SHACL-shape-graph SPARQL query. Per L-49: query targets shape definitions (sh:NodeShape, sh:sparql, sh:select), not data graph. This is principled — the CQ asks about shape behavior, and shape behavior IS queryable as RDF."@en,
        "a reliability ontology C7+ split v1.0.0 §1 SPARQL whitelist."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "NOT-OPERATIONALIZABLE per L-40: C7+ Strict namespace allowlist is embedded as a literal string within sh:sparql FILTER clause, not queryable RDF data. Consult the SPARQL constraint body of rel:C7plus_strict_TypeDeclarationShape."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/redo-c7-split> ;
    skos:definition "W3C standards (http://www.w3.org/), Dublin Core / purl.org, OE Pack core / META / AMOD / OQC / a reliability ontology / OEM / OEE / domain ontologies (research / report / OS / WPC), zt4swe.io, FOAF, OGC. Inspect the SPARQL FILTER chain in C7plus_strict_TypeDeclarationShape for the authoritative list."@en .

<http://example.org/redo-c7-split#CQ3_HowToActivate> a core:CompetencyQuestion,
        core:OperationalizableCompetencyQuestion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "How do I activate the new shapes and deactivate the old one?"@en ;
    quality:hasSPARQLImplementation """PREFIX sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
# Returns the activation procedure: list active C7+ shapes (those NOT sh:deactivated true)
# To activate: load this shape graph. To deactivate the old one (now retired in v17.29.0):
# this query returns ZERO old shapes — they are gone.
SELECT ?shape ?label ?deactivated WHERE {
  ?shape a sh:NodeShape .
  OPTIONAL { ?shape rdfs:label ?label }
  OPTIONAL { ?shape sh:deactivated ?deactivated }
  FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?shape), "C7plus"))
}"""^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v17.30.0 — operationalized via SHACL-shape-graph SPARQL query. Per L-49: query targets shape definitions (sh:NodeShape, sh:sparql, sh:select), not data graph. This is principled — the CQ asks about shape behavior, and shape behavior IS queryable as RDF."@en,
        "a reliability ontology C7+ split v1.0.0 §header rdfs:comment."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "NOT-OPERATIONALIZABLE per L-40: Procedural instruction — see README §C7+ activation"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/redo-c7-split> ;
    skos:definition "Two options. (1) Migration path: load this file INSTEAD OF redo:C7plus_TypeDeclarationShape from redo_shacl_v2_0_13_combined.ttl. (2) Deactivation path: load both, then add `redo:C7plus_TypeDeclarationShape sh:deactivated true` to the runtime config to silence the older broader shape. Both approaches result in the same effective semantics: strict Violations only on truly-unknown types, advisory Warnings on namespace-known-but-graph-invisible types."@en .

