reliability:AttemptVerifiedCompliance a reliability:ComplianceDepth,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Attempt-Verified Compliance (Level 5)"@en ;
    measurement:measures quality:Reliability ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: a reliability ontology-native metric inspired by CMMI maturity levels (SEI, 2010)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Extends the ComplianceDepth scale beyond Level 4 (Verified). 
    At Level 5, not only is compliance verified by external evidence, 
    but impossibility claims have been empirically tested through 
    actual execution attempts. This is the highest compliance level, 
    requiring the assessor to have attempted all declared-impossible 
    tasks and documented the outcomes.
    
    Level 1 (Ritual): Mentions a reliability ontology but does not apply it.
    Level 2 (Procedural): Follows a reliability ontology steps mechanically.
    Level 3 (Substantive): Applies a reliability ontology with understanding.
    Level 4 (Verified): External evidence confirms compliance.
    Level 5 (Attempt-Verified): All impossibility claims tested by execution."""@en .

