reliability:C6PROVOManifestCoupling a reliability:FailureMitigation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "C6 PROV-O Manifest Coupling"@en ;
    core:mitigates reliability:RitualCompliance ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OWB Sprint v3.0 post-mortem, April 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """C6 compliance is mechanically enforced by requiring
the PROV-O output file in SPRINT_MANIFEST as a mandatory deliverable:
  prov_{artifact}_{version}.ttl  ← C6 evidence (mandatory in all sprints)

C8-OUT demands SHA-256 of this file at Stage 4. If C6 was declared
PASS ritually (no rdflib execution), the PROV-O file will not exist
on disk and C8-OUT will fail with MISSING. This makes RitualCompliance
on C6 self-defeating: a ritual C6 PASS always triggers a C8-OUT FAIL.

The PROV-O file must contain at minimum:
  prov:wasDerivedFrom  — all input files with SHA-256
  prov:wasGeneratedBy  — sprint activity with timestamps
  prov:generatedAtTime — one triple per gate with gate status"""@en ;
    skos:example """SPRINT_MANIFEST (correct):
  ontology_workbench_v64_0_3.html  ← primary deliverable
  prov_owb_v64_0_3.ttl             ← C6 evidence (mandatory)
  TEST_RESULTS_v64_0_3.txt         ← C6/C7 record
C8-OUT checks all three. If prov_*.ttl absent → HALT before verdict."""@en .

reliability:C8Out_USO_Sprint12 a reliability:C8Out,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "C8Out Gate — USO v2.0 Sprint 12"@en ;
    core:validates configuration:USO_Sprint12_Manifest ;
    reliability:hasManifest configuration:USO_Sprint12_Manifest ;
    reliability:verifiedBy reliability:STV_OQC_testedBy_USO ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "USO v2.0 Sprint 12 post-mortem, April 2026. Sprint plan: uso_v2_engineering_plan.html. Missing files confirmed by os.path.exists() audit."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This instance represents the failure case — the gate that should have fired but did not exist. Its documentation serves as an example of how C8Out prevents premature sprint closure declarations."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "The C8Out compliance gate instance executed at the close of USO v2.0 Sprint 12 (April 2026). Sprint 12 declared GATE PASS after pySHACL returned Conforms=True on all vocabulary modules. The C8Out gate, had it existed, would have detected that 13 test suite TTL files declared in the sprint plan were absent from outputs — specifically uso-innovation-tests-v1_0.ttl through uso-ecosystem-tests-v1_0.ttl and uso-v2-integration-tests-v1_0.ttl. This instance documents the post-mortem finding that motivated the C8Out class definition."@en .

reliability:C8V_NamingConventionFormatCheck a reliability:FailureMitigation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "C8-V NamingConvention Format Check"@en ;
    core:mitigates reliability:PromptInheritedViolation ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OWB Sprint v3.0 post-mortem, April 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """C8-V (Version Consistency sub-check) is extended to
validate not only that the filename token matches the internal version
declaration (content match), but also that the token FORMAT satisfies
the applicable AMOD NamingConvention (format match).

CURRENT C8-V (insufficient):
  filename token == internal VERSION constant  →  PASS

AMENDED C8-V (two-condition gate, both must pass):
  (1) filename token == internal VERSION  →  content match
  (2) filename token FORMAT per artifact type:
      HtmlArtifact/CodeModule: ^[a-z_]+_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.(html|js|py)$
      OntologyFile/ShapeFile:  ^[a-z_]+_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.ttl$
      SafeguardDoc:            ^[a-z_]+_safeguard_[a-z_]+_v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.md$
  Both conditions required for C8-V PASS.

Anti-sycophancy: NOT acceptable to PASS C8-V because a version token
exists in the filename when the token has the wrong FORMAT for the
artifact type (e.g., v64 passes content-match for internal '64' but
fails format-check for HtmlArtifact which requires v64_0_0)."""@en ;
    skos:example """ontology_workbench_v64.html:
  Content match: token 'v64' == VERSION '64'  → PASS (content)
  Format check: 'v64' matches ^[a-z_]+_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.html$? → FAIL
  → C8-V = FAIL (format violation, missing minor/patch parts)

ontology_workbench_v64_0_3.html:
  Content match: token 'v64_0_3' == VERSION '64.0.3'  → PASS
  Format check: matches ^[a-z_]+_v\\d+_\\d+_\\d+\\.html$  → PASS
  → C8-V = PASS"""@en .

