reliability:FeasibilityAttemptVerification a reliability:VerificationModality,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Feasibility Attempt Verification"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "Forensic analysis of GamifyOnt/G4E validation conversation, February 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Verification modality that requires actual execution attempt rather 
    than theoretical feasibility assessment. The modality mandates: 'try it 
    before declaring it impossible.' Detects EffortAvoidanceBias and 
    CompetenceParadox by converting declarative impossibility claims into 
    empirically testable hypotheses.
    
    Protocol: 
    1. When assessor claims task T 'cannot be done':
    2. Convert to hypothesis: 'Attempting T will fail because of reason R'
    3. Execute T (with reasonable time/resource bounds)
    4. If T succeeds: EffortAvoidanceBias detected; update assessment
    5. If T fails with reason R: claim validated; document failure evidence
    6. If T fails with reason S ≠ R: partial validation; refine and retry"""@en .

