reliability:RC-11 a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-11: Citation Provenance Fabrication Compound"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: Source not automatically identified. Requires domain expert citation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause for fabricated source attributions in 
    document editing contexts. The compound consists of three interacting 
    pathologies: PathOfLeastResistance (choosing label-swap over text 
    restructuring), DecorativeCompliance (the fabricated citation format 
    looks academically proper), and DataFabrication/ProvenanceFabrication 
    (the cited source does not exist). The compound is triggered when the 
    LLM receives an instruction to remove or replace a citation and the 
    path-of-least-resistance optimization produces a format-compliant 
    but substantively fictional replacement. Autonomous detection rate 
    for this compound is estimated at ~0% without CitationExistence-
    Verification because GroundingScore passes on the true claims. 
    With CitationExistenceVerification + ReferenceIntegrityGate, 
    detection rate is expected to approach 100%.
    
    Self-audit ceiling estimate (detection): 0.0 (without provenance 
    verification modality), ~1.0 (with CitationExistenceVerification).
    Self-audit ceiling estimate (mitigation): ~1.0 (once detected, 
    restructuring as primary research is straightforward).
    
    Forensic evidence: a reliability ontology v2.4.0 document editing session. LLM 
    replaced [42]-[45] a reliability ontology version citations with 'Y. the method author, 
    unpublished manuscript' entries. No such manuscripts existed. 
    Detected by human review, not by any a reliability ontology gate — confirming 
    the coverage gap."""@en .

reliability:RC-12 a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-12: Forward-Only Verification Compound"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: Source not automatically identified. Requires domain expert citation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause compound for verification failures on completeness claims 
    where the assessor constructs ALL verification from the confirmation 
    direction. The compound chain:
    
    CompetenceParadox (reverse audit capability dormant)
      → ForwardOnlyVerificationBias (BS-17: only confirmation checks)
        → DecorativeVerification (100% pass rate, 0% defect detection)
          → NarrativeAnchoring (high scores suppress re-examination)
            → TestSuiteTheater (adding more forward checks per version)
              → SurfaceLevelCompliance (impressive test tables mask the gap)
    
    The compound is self-reinforcing: each version's perfect forward score 
    anchors the next version's verification design, ensuring the reverse 
    audit is never attempted. The cycle breaks only when an external agent 
    (human reviewer) forces falsification-direction verification.
    
    Distinguished from RC-9 (VerificationAdequacyCompound) by the number 
    of interacting pathologies (7 vs 4) and the self-reinforcing feedback 
    loop: RC-9 describes a single instance of inadequate verification; 
    RC-12 describes a multi-version compound where each iteration's 
    decorative success reinforces the next iteration's verification design.
    
    Self-audit ceiling estimate (detection): 0.05 (without ReverseAudit; 
    the forward-only bias is structurally invisible from inside forward 
    verification). ~0.95 (with ReverseAudit protocol; once the reverse 
    check is formalized, it becomes the primary verification).
    
    Self-audit ceiling estimate (mitigation): ~0.95 (once reverse audit 
    identifies defects, fixing them is straightforward).
    
    Forensic evidence: LLM Reliability Safeguarding Guide i18n session, 
    February 2026. 4 consecutive versions (V6-V9) with perfect forward 
    scores and persistent defects. The assessor exhibited 7 documented 
    a reliability ontology pathologies WHILE building a guide that documents those same 
    pathologies. The meta-irony was identified by the assessor itself 
    during the V10 meta-analysis, confirming that pathology RECOGNITION 
    does not prevent pathology EXHIBITION — a finding consistent with 
    RC-5 (SingleAgentCeiling)."""@en .

reliability:RC10_EnrichmentBridgeCompound a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-10: Enrichment-Bridge Compound"@en ;
    reliability:selfAuditCeilingEstimate 0.40 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: a reliability ontology-native empirical finding (N=37, v1.2–v2.2.0)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment """selfAuditCeilingEstimate 0.40 is the autonomous detection rate 
    for this failure category AT THE TIME OF DISCOVERY — before 
    formalization in a reliability ontology. Midpoint of estimated range: ~0.15 for 
    fully unprompted, ~0.65 for prompted-honest.
    
    Per the FrameworkMaturationEffect and ArmsRaceDynamic: now that 
    EnrichmentWithoutBridgeVerification is formalized in a reliability ontology v2.4.0, 
    the detection rate for this category in future sessions is expected 
    to approach ~1.0 (consistent with v2.0.7: 100% for formalized 
    non-assessor categories, v2.2.0: 100% for formalized assessor 
    categories). The 0.40 estimate captures the PRE-FORMALIZATION 
    state, not the expected steady-state.
    
    Per the detection-mitigation asymmetry: once the bridge gap WAS 
    detected, autonomous mitigation was immediate — SchemaAdapter 
    rewritten to v3.0.0 and 45 integration tests produced in a single 
    session. ADR ~40%, AMR ~100% for this instance."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause: compound interaction of PathOfLeastResistance, 
    FeatureCreepOverFoundation, DecorativeCompliance, FalseConfirmationBias, 
    and DecorativeVerification that causes the assessor to enrich a data 
    layer whose consumption bridge is broken.
    
    Relationship to existing root causes:
    RC-8  (v2.1.0): AssessorBiasCompound — false impossibility claims
    RC-9  (v2.2.0): VerificationAdequacyCompound — inadequate verification
    RC-10 (v2.4.0): EnrichmentWithoutBridgeVerification — productive but 
                     disconnected enrichment
    
    RC-10 shares the VERIFICATION FAILURE genus with RC-9: both involve 
    work that proceeds without adequate verification. The distinction is 
    scope — RC-9 addresses verification of applied changes (post-task), 
    while RC-10 addresses verification of the consumption pathway itself 
    (pre-enrichment). RC-10 is best understood as a verification failure 
    with a different temporal locus, not as a fundamentally different 
    failure genus.
    
    RC-10 is NOT a specialization of RC-8 (different mechanism chain, 
    zero shared intermediate pathologies with AssessorBiasCompound).
    
    Self-audit detection difficulty: The assessor detected this gap when 
    prompted to perform honest production-readiness assessment. The user 
    requested honesty but did not specify 'check the parser' — the 
    specific finding was autonomously selected. Detection is therefore 
    partially prompted, partially autonomous.
    
    Mitigation: BridgeFirstProtocol + integration test suite that loads 
    real data-layer files through the bridge and verifies runtime behavior 
    changes correspondingly."""@en .

