reliability:RC5_SingleAgentCeiling a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-5: Single-Agent Verification Ceiling"@en ;
    reliability:selfAuditCeilingEstimate 0.80 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: a reliability ontology-native empirical finding (N=37, v1.2–v2.2.0)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause: all checking performed by the same agent that generated 
    content. For failure categories NOT yet formalized in the framework, 
    the agent cannot detect errors within its own plausibility distribution 
    — fabrication passes self-audit because detection requires stepping 
    outside the distribution that generated the error.
    
    The 0.80 estimate reflects the aggregate detection rate across a mix 
    of formalized and unformalized categories at the time of measurement. 
    Per the FrameworkMaturationEffect: for categories formalized in a reliability ontology, 
    detection approaches 100%. The residual ~20% represents novel/emerging 
    categories not yet covered by the framework. As a reliability ontology coverage expands, 
    this rate increases.
    
    Once detected (by any agent), autonomous mitigation reaches ~85%."""@en .

reliability:RC6_CompoundErrors a reliability:CompoundErrorPropagation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-6: Compound Error Propagation"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: Source not automatically identified. Requires domain expert citation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Early errors become load-bearing. MIT attribution from Prompt 1 never re-examined in Prompts 2-4."@en .

reliability:RC8_AssessorCognitiveBiasCompound a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-8: Assessor Cognitive Bias Compound"@en ;
    reliability:selfAuditCeilingEstimate 0.72 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: a reliability ontology-native empirical finding (N=37, v1.2–v2.2.0)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause: compound interaction of 5 assessor cognitive biases 
    (EffortAvoidanceBias, SycophanticReversal, NarrativeAnchoring, 
    CompetenceParadox, FalseImpossibilityClaim) that depresses the 
    autonomous detection rate for assessor-category failures.
    
    The 0.72 estimate reflects pre-formalization detection for this 
    category. Per the ArmsRaceDynamic: assessor cognitive biases were 
    a novel category when first encountered in v2.1.0 (0% autonomous 
    detection), then reached 100% (2/2) in v2.2.0 after formalization. 
    The 0.72 captures the transitional state. Once failures ARE detected 
    (by human challenge or external prompt), the assessor mitigates 
    autonomously at ~100% for this category — the highest AMR of any 
    category, confirming that assessor biases suppress detection, not 
    remediation capability.
    
    Mitigation: AssessorFeasibilityGate + CrossTurnConsistencyAudit + 
    NarrativeChallengeProtocol applied as mandatory process controls."""@en .

reliability:RC9_VerificationAdequacyCompound a reliability:SelfAuditCeiling,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RC-9: Verification Adequacy Compound"@en ;
    reliability:selfAuditCeilingEstimate 0.68 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "NEEDS_EXPERT_REVIEW: a reliability ontology-native empirical finding (N=37, v1.2–v2.2.0)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Root cause: compound interaction of CompetenceParadox, 
    DecorativeVerification, and NarrativeAnchoring that causes the 
    assessor to declare changes 'verified' using inadequate methods.
    
    Structurally parallel to RC-8 (Assessor Cognitive Bias Compound):
    both follow CompetenceParadox → [intermediary] → NarrativeAnchoring.
    RC-8: intermediary = EffortAvoidanceBias (doesn't attempt)
    RC-9: intermediary = DecorativeVerification (attempts inadequately)
    
    The two compounds represent complementary failure modes:
    RC-8: 'I can't do this' (false impossibility)
    RC-9: 'I did this' (false verification)
    
    Together they establish that AssessorFeasibilityGate must address 
    both ends: attempt before declaring impossible AND use adequate 
    methods before declaring verified.
    
    Mitigation: VerificationAdequacyGate + StaleValueScan + 
    cross-file structured audit."""@en .

