reliability:ReferenceIntegrityGate a reliability:ComplianceGate,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Reference Integrity Gate"@en ;
    core:detects reliability:DataFabrication ;
    core:validates reliability:Artifact ;
    reliability:gateStage reliability:PostGenerationStage ;
    reliability:mitigatesPathology reliability:ProvenanceFabrication ;
    reliability:performedBy reliability:Agent_ReliabilityEngineer ;
    reliability:verifiedBy reliability:EmpiricalTest_HallucinationBenchmark ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "Cooper, R.G. (1990). Stage-Gate Systems. Business Horizons, 33(3). Adapted for a reliability ontology verification."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """A compliance gate that enforces citation integrity at 
    two critical points: (1) GENERATION — every bibliographic entry in the 
    output must correspond to a source that exists and can be independently 
    verified, and (2) MODIFICATION — when a reference is removed, replaced, 
    or restructured, the gate enforces a decision protocol that prevents 
    provenance fabrication.
    
    The gate implements the ReferenceModificationProtocol:
    
    TRIGGER: Any instruction to add, remove, or replace a citation.
    
    DECISION TREE:
      IF adding a new citation:
        → Verify the source exists (DOI, URL, file, database lookup)
        → IF source cannot be verified → mark [UNVERIFIED] or restructure 
          as inline primary research
      IF removing a citation:
        → Are the findings primary research reported in this document?
          YES → Restructure text to present inline with no external citation.
                Reference entry becomes: 'Primary research reported in this 
                paper/report (Section X).'
          NO  → Is there an alternative real source?
                YES → Replace with verified alternative.
                NO  → Remove both the inline citation and reference entry.
      IF replacing a citation:
        → Verify the replacement source exists before writing it.
        → NEVER swap a citation label without verifying the target exists.
    
    BLOCKED PATTERN: Replacing a real citation with a fabricated 
    'unpublished manuscript' or invented journal reference. This is the 
    PathOfLeastResistance → DecorativeCompliance compound that produces 
    ProvenanceFabrication.
    
    ENFORCEMENT: PostGeneration stage. Every reference in the final 
    bibliography must pass CitationExistenceVerification before delivery."""@en ;
    skos:example """User: 'Remove all a reliability ontology version references from citations [42]-[45].'
    
    WITHOUT gate: LLM swaps '[42] a reliability ontology v2.1.0, Assessor Cognitive Bias...' 
    with '[42] Y. the method author, unpublished manuscript...' — fabricated source.
    
    WITH gate: LLM recognizes [42]-[45] are primary research, restructures 
    as '[42] Primary research reported in this paper (Section 7).' and 
    removes inline [42] markers where the findings are already described 
    in the text body."""@en .

