reliability:SafeguardInheritanceProtocol a reliability:FailureMitigation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Safeguard Inheritance Protocol"@en ;
    core:mitigates reliability:SafeguardVariantIncompleteness ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OWB Sprint v3.0 post-mortem, April 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """All a reliability ontology safeguard variant documents must include an
explicit INHERITANCE DECLARATION at the top, immediately after the
USAGE MODE section, listing every base-level gate and pre-condition
that the variant inherits unchanged:

  ═══ INHERITED FROM redo_safeguard_base_v1.3.md (all variants) ═══
  The following apply to this variant without modification:
    - VerificationAdequacyGate Q1/Q2/Q3 (Stage 1 BLOCKING pre-condition)
    - Session Refresh Protocol (UNCONDITIONAL when >20 exchanges)
    - Bridge-First Protocol (when data layer exists)
    - Stage 1 Manifest NamingConvention Validation
    - C6 PROV-O Manifest Coupling (prov_*.ttl in SPRINT_MANIFEST)
    - C8-V NamingConvention Format Check (3-part for TTL/HTML/JS;
      2-part DOT for safeguard MD)
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The variant sections document ONLY what differs from the base.

Machine-readable form: sprint manifests should declare
  redo:this_sprint redo:activatedSafeguard redo:html_js_variant ;
                   redo:inheritsBase      redo:safeguard_base .
enabling SPARQL to retrieve all applicable requirements."""@en ;
    skos:example """redo_safeguard_html_js_v1.3.md now opens with an explicit
inheritance block listing all base pre-conditions before the HTML/JS-
specific C1-C8 rules. An LLM reading only the variant still encounters
the VerificationAdequacyGate requirement on page 1."""@en .

