    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "USO v2.0 Sprint 12 remediation session, April 2026. C-SC gate result: 26/26 manifest files present, pySHACL Conforms=True V=0 on all. Schwaber, K. & Sutherland, J. (2020). The Scrum Guide."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Paired with C8Out_USO_Sprint12. Where C8Out documents the failure mode, SprintCC_USO_Sprint12 documents the corrected execution — the checklist run after all 13 missing files were built and confirmed."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "The SprintClosureChecklist gate instance retrospectively applied to USO v2.0 Sprint 12 (April 2026). When applied in the remediation session, the checklist parsed and pySHACL-validated all 26 manifest files (12 vocabulary modules, 12 test suites, 1 integration suite, 1 alignment TTL) and reported GATE PASS with Conforms=True and V=0 on all entries. This instance demonstrates the gate operating correctly on a complete manifest, in contrast to the Sprint 12 original which lacked the test suite files."@en .

reliability:Stage1ManifestValidationProtocol a reliability:FailureMitigation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 1 Manifest Validation Protocol"@en ;
    core:mitigates reliability:CompoundErrorPropagation,
        reliability:PromptInheritedViolation ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "OWB Sprint v3.0 post-mortem, April 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """At Stage 1 Pre-flight, BEFORE any sprint work begins,
the LLM must validate every SPRINT_MANIFEST entry against its applicable
AMOD NamingConvention pattern:
  HtmlArtifact:     {name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.html  (3-part underscore)
  OntologyFile:     {prefix}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl  (3-part underscore)
  ShapeFile:        {prefix}_shacl_v{M}_{m}_{p}.ttl (3-part underscore)
  SafeguardDoc:     {prefix}_safeguard_{variant}_v{M}.{m}.md (2-part DOT)
  CodeModule:       {name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.{ext}  (3-part underscore)

If any entry violates its NamingConvention: (1) flag with C8-V gate ID,
(2) propose corrected filename, (3) block sprint execution until user
confirms the correction. User-supplied entries are NOT exempt."""@en ;
    skos:example """Sprint prompt: SPRINT_MANIFEST: ontology_workbench_v64.html
Stage 1 check: HtmlArtifact pattern requires _v{M}_{m}_{p}.html.
'v64' has only 1 part (M only). Correct: ontology_workbench_v64_0_0.html.
Block sprint. Notify user. Await confirmation before proceeding."""@en .

reliability:StaleValueScan a reliability:VerificationModality,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Stale Value Scan"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "Forensic analysis of a reliability ontology v2.1.0 HTML update session, February 2026."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition """Verification modality that searches for values that SHOULD NOT be 
    present, complementing standard verification that searches for values 
    that SHOULD be present. Essential for count-update operations where 
    the failure mode is incomplete replacement rather than missing insertion.
    
    Protocol:
    1. Enumerate all values that were replaced (old → new)
    2. Search all output files for the OLD values
    3. For each match, determine if contextual (quotation, historical 
       reference, version-specific note) or stale (should have been updated)
    4. Flag stale matches as verification failures
    
    This modality directly addresses DecorativeVerification: it forces 
    the assessor to look for what should be absent, not just confirm 
    what should be present."""@en .

