    skos:definition "A mitigation strategy in which any downstream artifact derived from a labeled source inherits the source's trust label (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/MISSING/FABRICATED), and any LOW/MISSING/FABRICATED label is propagated as a warning in the derived artifact's metadata. Operationalizes the existing trust-tier discipline."@en .

