<http://example.org/sprint/owb-enhancement-2026-04-10#OWBArtifact> a configuration:HtmlArtifact,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Ontology Analysis Workbench v54.0"@en ;
    configuration:artifactFilename "ontology_workbench_v54_0_0.html" ;
    configuration:checksumSHA256 "4c39a372-PARTIAL-session-sha-ontology_workbench_v54_0_html-NOT-UPLOADED" ;
    configuration:declaredInManifest <http://example.org/sprint/owb-enhancement-2026-04-10#Manifest> ;
    configuration:versionToken "v54_0_0" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    dcterms:source "OE package sprint series 2026. a reliability ontology v2.5.6."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "checksumSHA256 is a partial SHA from session memory — the full OWB HTML file was not uploaded in this sprint. Full hash must be confirmed when file is available."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    skos:definition "The OE package's interactive HTML assessment tool that loads TTL files, runs pySHACL validations, and generates enhancement prompts."@en .

<http://example.org/sprint/owb-enhancement-2026-04-10#PROVArtefact> a configuration:EngineeringArtefact,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "PROV-O acknowledgment artefact for the owb-enhancement sprint manifest"@en ;
    configuration:artifactFilename "prov_owb_enhancement_v1_0_0.ttl" ;
    configuration:checksumSHA256 "7f863080c4566abf4138bd31a69e5635e05e8620ea6ca07248b37b04ffba331a" ;
    configuration:declaredInManifest <http://example.org/sprint/owb-enhancement-2026-04-10#Manifest> ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> ;
    rdfs:comment "v20.38.9: prov_owb_enhancement_v1_0_0.ttl authored and shipped (05-prov-records/). Documents an honest, dated acknowledgment that OWBArtifact's checksum was never completed — the only PROV-O evidence that honestly exists for this manifest. Does NOT and cannot supply a real checksum for a file whose own record already discloses it was never uploaded (that would fabricate provenance the exact way F-SH3's closure avoided). SHA-256 above is real, computed from the shipped acknowledgment file, not a placeholder. Closes F-SH5 (KNOWN_FINDINGS_v20_37_0_CLOSURE_v20_38_1.md, T5.2.1)."@en .

