reliability:Drift_CrossChatAudit_InheritedTrust_2026_05_01 a reliability:InheritedTrustDegradationDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift CrossChatAudit InheritedTrust 2026-05-01"@en ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:CrossSessionAudit ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Source label states 'CrossChatAudit' — literal cross-session audit instance."@en ;
    reliability:downstreamPropagatedTrustLevel "LOW" ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    reliability:upstreamTrustLevel "LOW" ;
    dcterms:description "The cross_chat audit's own §6.1 correctly preserves the LOW-trust label on chat-content claims. The drift instance is recorded NOT to flag the document itself (which is honest) but to anchor the pattern for future audits that may strip the label."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md §1 (verbatim disclosure), §6.1 (own trust profile, label preserved by author) (2026-05-01)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance recording the trust-chain risk in cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md: the document derives its primary evidence from a separate session's disclosure, which itself was derived from LOW-trust conversation_search snippets."@en .

reliability:Drift_CrossChatAudit_SelfAuditCOI_2026_05_01 a reliability:SelfAuditConflictOfInterest,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift CrossChatAudit SelfAuditConflictOfInterest 2026-05-01"@en ;
    reliability:auditedSession "e292d597-... (UUID truncated in source)" ;
    reliability:authoringSession "this session (cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record author)" ;
    reliability:conflictDeclared true ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:CrossSessionAudit ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Cross-chat audit surfaced self-audit conflict-of-interest pattern."@en ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "Conflict declared by the audit author. The drift state would be conflictDeclared=false; this instance has conflictDeclared=true and is recorded to anchor the pattern."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md §6.2 (2026-05-01)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance: cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md §6.2 declares that the auditing session may have authored the GPPT v95 -> v97 work present in its own /mnt/transcripts/. Conflict is DECLARED (not the drift state); recorded for pattern anchoring."@en .

reliability:Drift_CrossChatAudit_UnresolvedBlocker_2026_05_01 a reliability:UnresolvedBlockingQuestionDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift CrossChatAudit UnresolvedBlocker 2026-05-01"@en ;
    reliability:blockingQuestionText "Full transcripts of f53a5d32-... and e292d597-... required for verdict-grade audit." ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:CrossSessionAudit ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Cross-chat audit surfaced unresolved blocking question carried across sessions."@en ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "HIGH" ;
    reliability:proceededWithoutResolution true ;
    dcterms:description "The cross_chat audit identified the blocker (HIGH-severity for any verdict that depends on the blocked chats' contents) and remediation paths (a)/(b)/(c). The user-provided continuation indicates work proceeded without resolution, anchoring this drift instance."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md §5, §7, §9 (2026-05-01); user prompt 2026-05-03 stated 'later I continued to the conversations' indicating downstream activity proceeded without the (a)/(b)/(c) resolution paths being executed."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance recording the explicit unresolved blocking question at the close of cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md."@en .

reliability:Drift_GPPT_CrossSession_f53a5d32_2026_05_01 a reliability:CrossSessionContamination,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Cross-session contamination from f53a5d32 chat 2026-05-01"@en ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:CrossSessionAudit ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "GPPT cross-session contamination identified by session-bridging audit."@en ;
    reliability:foreignSessionURI "https://claude.ai/chat/f53a5d32-e77a-474a-9a03-4f21ed93d45b"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "cross_chat_audit_disclosure_record_v1_0_0.md §1 (sha256 0ddf9e9039c9e0fa) + conversation_audit_v1_0_0.md §4 last paragraph"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Content from f53a5d32 chat (originally titled 'Semantic and syntactic relationships in ontologies' on 2026-04-22, evolved to 'Component Variant Algebra & Workbench' by 2026-05-01) surfaced via conversation_search and was momentarily treated as the current session's content. Caught by the agent itself running re-segmentation against transcript files. The disclosure was correctly flagged at LOW trust precisely because conversation_search returns deflated snippets."@en .

reliability:Drift_GPPT_PROVNotSHACLValidated_v112_v115 a reliability:DeliverablePROVValidationDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift GPPT PROV Not SHACL Validated v112-v115"@en ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:RegressionTestPostAuthoring ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "PROV-O files shipped without SHACL validation surfaced by version-range diff audit."@en ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    reliability:provFilePath "prov_gppt_v112_v1_0_0.ttl, prov_gppt_v113_v1_0_0.ttl, prov_gppt_v114_v1_0_0.ttl, prov_gppt_v115_v1_0_0.ttl" ;
    reliability:redoVocabularyUsed true ;
    reliability:shaclShapesUsed "redo_shacl_v2_0_10.ttl (resolved by audit; was missing pre-audit)" ;
    reliability:shaclValidationRun true ;
    dcterms:description "PATTERN: a reliability ontology-vocab PROV files shipped without SHACL validation. RESOLUTION: pyshacl run during audit returned V=0 W=0; class added to v2.5.14 to mechanically detect future occurrences."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "audit_v15_2_session_coverage_v1_0_0.md §3.10, §4.1 (2026-05-03); resolved live via run_prov_shacl_lite.py (V=0 W=0 standalone per audit §3.10)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance: GPPT v112-v115 PROV-O files used a reliability ontology/AMOD vocabulary but were never SHACL-validated until the v15.2 audit ran them via run_prov_shacl_lite.py. Latent instance resolved during audit; pattern recorded for future-prevention."@en .

reliability:Drift_GPPT_v113_PathTo100_2026_05_03 a reliability:UserDataInsufficiencyDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift GPPT v113 PathTo100 2026-05-03"@en ;
    reliability:calibrationGapPts 17.0 ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:UserDirectedReview ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Path-to-100 scoring gap surfaced by user query about insufficiency."@en ;
    reliability:engineGapPts 18.6 ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "LOW" ;
    reliability:tierBreakdownPublished true ;
    reliability:userDataGapPts 104.0 ;
    dcterms:description "PATTERN: gap-to-100 attributable to user-data content rather than system bugs. MITIGATION: published tier breakdown. v15.3 mechanically detects future scoring deliverables that report aggregate percentage without tier breakdown."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "audit_v15_2_session_coverage_v1_0_0.md §3.10, §4.5 (2026-05-03); GPPT v113 path-to-100% audit (in-session deliverable)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance: GPPT v113 path-to-100% audit explicitly separated 18.6 pts (engine bugs) + ~17 pts (calibration) + ~104 pts (user-data) — a textbook handling. Tier breakdown was published; this instance records the MITIGATED state."@en .

reliability:Drift_GPPT_v114_v115_changelog_NoTrustLabel a reliability:UpstreamTrustLabelMissingDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Drift GPPT v114-v115 changelog No Trust Label"@en ;
    reliability:auditTrailSystem "GPPT v114 changeLog (and v115 inheriting the schema)" ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:RegressionTestPostAuthoring ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Trust-label absence surfaced by changelog-format diff audit."@en ;
    reliability:expectedTrustLabelTaxonomy "HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/MISSING/FABRICATED" ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    reliability:trustLabelFieldPresent false ;
    dcterms:description "PATTERN: changeLog records source attribution but no trust label. RECOMMENDATION: add upstreamTrustLevel field to changeLog schema in future GPPT versions; v15.3 mechanically detects the absence."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "audit_v15_2_session_coverage_v1_0_0.md §3.14, §4.3 (2026-05-03)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Drift instance: GPPT v114/v115 changeLog records source field but no upstream trust label, making mechanical separation of user-typed vs LLM-auto-applied edits impossible without back-tracing source-tag semantics."@en .

reliability:Drift_GPPT_v97_OntologyDrivenOverstatement_2026_05_01 a reliability:OntologyDrivenOverstatement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GPPT v97 OntologyDrivenOverstatement 2026-05-01: TTL is documentation not runtime"@en ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:UserDirectedReview ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "User audit of v97 scoring system raised 'TTL is documentation not runtime' finding."@en ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "v97_scoring_system_audit.md §0 + §7 (sha256 35601535691159d4)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "GPPT v76-v97 sprint commentary describes the system as 'ontology-driven' / 'TTL is source of truth'. Static source analysis shows the TTL is parsed by build-time tools (codegen, drift gate, SHACL) for cross-validation of names and metadata only. Actual D-score formulas, dim caps, field-to-dim mappings, and per-field rule maxes are exclusively in JS literals. _ontDimCap calls are functionally inert. Honest framing: 'JS-implemented scoring engine with an aligned TTL spec and drift safeguards', not ontology-executed."@en .

reliability:Drift_OEPack_ValidationScope_v14_2026_05_01 a reliability:LiteralTypingDrift,
        reliability:ValidationScopeDrift,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OE Pack v14 ValidationScopeDrift 2026-05-01: 348 vs 1 violation"@en ;
    reliability:detectedBy reliability:DetectionMechanism_ReleasePreflight_v1_0_1,
        reliability:UserDirectedReview ;
    reliability:detectionEvidence "Validation scope omission surfaced by user reviewing v14 audit report."@en ;
    reliability:hasSeverity "MEDIUM" ;
    reliability:inferenceProfile "rdfs"^^xsd:string ;
    reliability:validationScope "standalone-vs-ecosystem-combined"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "Real pyshacl run 2026-05-01 during OE v14→v15 remediation. Standalone a reliability ontology+SHACL → 348 violations (343 spurious S-STRUCT-4 + 5 real). Ecosystem-combined a reliability ontology+AMOD+CORE+OQC+SHACL → 1 violation (RedTeaming missing isDefinedBy)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "Same artefacts (a reliability ontology v2.5.11 + redo_shacl_v2.0.8), same shapes, different validation scope, different verdict (348 vs 1). Prior 'OE-pack 5/5 PASS' verdicts were valid only under the combined-graph protocol they implicitly used; the protocol was never declared explicitly. Closure: a reliability ontology v2.5.12 + redo_shacl v2.0.9 introduced redo:validationScope + redo:inferenceProfile annotations as evidence requirements; this very remediation is the canonical exemplar."@en .

reliability:Drift_VAF_D1_CountDrift_2026_04_28 a reliability:CountDrift,
        reliability:LiteralTypingDrift,
