reliability:STV_OQC_testedBy_USO a reliability:SemanticTargetVerification,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Semantic Target Verification — OQC testedBy USO modules"@en ;
    core:detects reliability:FalseConfirmationBias ;
    reliability:hasConfidenceLevel 1.00 ;
    reliability:triggersAlert reliability:FalseConfirmationBias_Example ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    dcterms:source "USO v2.0 OQC remediation session, April 2026. OQC OntologyMustBeTestedShape: 14/14 PASS after test suite files created. W3C OWL 2 Primer: reference integrity."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This instance demonstrates the distinction between a triple that is syntactically valid (meta:testedBy <IRI>) and one that is semantically grounded (the target IRI resolves to an actual file). The former satisfies the SHACL minCount=1 shape; only the latter constitutes real test coverage."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/reliability> ;
    skos:definition "The SemanticTargetVerification instance applied to the USO v2.0 module headers during the Sprint 12 OQC remediation. Each module declared meta:testedBy pointing to a test suite IRI (e.g., test:USO_Inno_TestSuite_v1). The STV gate confirmed that each target IRI resolved to a loadable, parseable TTL file via g.parse(). Before the test suite files were built, these triples were dangling references — structurally valid but semantically empty. After the 13 test suite files were produced, all target IRIs resolved and the STV gate passed."@en .

