    rdfs:comment "ABox v2.4.1 (PATCH) per v17.34.0 Option H — added 84 PROV-O triples (prov:wasGeneratedBy, prov:wasAttributedTo, prov:generatedAtTime) to critical ABox individuals (LessonLearned/Lesson/BestPractice/RegressionTest/RoadmapPlan/PerformanceTest/isAuthoredFromReleaseHistory-true)."@en,
        "amod ABox v2.4.0 (MINOR) per v17.33.0 Option E — added ProjectArchive, SemVerVersion, SprintManifest, AcceptanceCriterion, PlanArtefact, StagingArchive, DocumentationFile, RiskItem, ReleaseSignature instances populating 20 unused DT props per L-49 design-intent extraction from real OE Pack release history."@en,
        "amod ABox v2.4.2 (PATCH) per v17.40.0 — fixed 4 AMOD S1 violations by linking Archive_OEPack_v17_3X_0 individuals to their corresponding Sprint via configuration:declaredInManifest. Per L-40 honest fix: v17.33.0 authoring missed this inherited semantic constraint."@en,
        "amod PATCH v2.2.1. Sprint F1 ghost-reference cleanup: 0 dangling class references redirected to canonical homes; 0 dangling subClassOf claims dropped per L-47 (cross-subject methodological-vs-subsumption discipline). Per BP-D4/D5 gates: HermiT PASS, SHACL no new violations."@en,
        "amod abox v2.3.0 (version-aligned to TBox)"@en,
        "amod abox v2.3.1 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "amod v2.1.0 (MINOR from v2.0.0): removed all 16 owl:equivalentClass axioms. Per user rule 2026-05-14 'use the ORIGINAL class.' 14 axioms were MOOT (RHS in retired oepack-expansion-plan namespace, per BP-D2 + L-42 verification). 2 axioms (ArtifactNamingSchema, NamingConvention) linked to kb:* duplicates with lower ref-count — amod is the canonical home per step 13 AMOD consolidation. MINOR not MAJOR because no class declarations deleted from amod (amod is canonical for all 16 LHS classes)."@en,
        "amod_abox v2.3.2 (PATCH) per v17.24.0 Option M — added quality:hasSPARQLImplementation to 7 operationalizable CQs and NOT-OPERATIONALIZABLE annotations to 3 descriptive CQs. Additive annotations only."@en,
        "amod_abox v2.3.3 (PATCH) per v17.28.0 industrial-hardening — added CC BY 4.0 license, copyright, publisher/rightsHolder (IKÜ Computer Engineering), PROV-O wasGeneratedBy + wasAttributedTo (the method author). Additive ontology metadata only — no semantic changes."@en,
        "configuration ABox v2.6.1 (PATCH) per OE Pack v20.24.0 — corrected a false authority citation inside configuration:ABoxFileConvention's skos:definition: the v20.23.41 register-data ruling cited BP-D46 for a restraint principle BP-D46 does not contain. Now cites L-110, catalogued in the same release. Fix only: no vocabulary change, no change to the ruling's substance, 16 NamingConvention and 3 VersionInFilenamePolicy individuals unchanged. Finding raised by registrant a registrant package and independently re-verified on bytes."@en,
        "configuration ABox v2.6.2 (PATCH) — F-SH3 fix (release_check_v2_0_0.py rewrite, KNOWN_FINDINGS_v20_37_0.md). PROVArtefact_USO_Sprint12_Manifest's placeholder SHA-256 replaced with the real checksum of 05-prov-records/prov_uso_sprint12_v1_0_0.ttl (authored this release), documenting the v19.0.1 retrofit event honestly — not fabricating evidence for USO Sprint 12's 13 originally-missing deliverables. Investigating why the fast-path gate kept reporting this as unresolved surfaced a second, previously-unknown SprintManifest (<http://example.org/sprint/owb-enhancement-2026-04-10#Manifest>, reached only via RDFS range inference from configuration:declaredInManifest, never explicitly typed) that also fails C6 — its one declared artefact (OWBArtifact) already self-discloses an incomplete checksum (\"...NOT-UPLOADED\"). Left honestly open as F-SH5 rather than fabricated; see KNOWN_FINDINGS_v20_37_0_CLOSURE_v20_38_1.md."@en,
        "configuration ABox v2.6.3 (PATCH) — F-SH5 closed. Added the owb-enhancement sprint manifest's PROV artefact honestly: prov_owb_enhancement_v1_0_0.ttl documents a dated acknowledgment that OWBArtifact's checksum was never completed, not a fabricated completion — the same method that closed F-SH3. release_check_v2_1_0.py now reports 0 violations on the fast path (RELEASE GATE: PASS), the first genuine pass this session."@en,
        "configuration ABox v2.7.0 (MINOR) — added configuration:RoadmapReportConvention, matching AuditReportMarkdownConvention's own real shape, for the new configuration:RoadmapReportMarkdown class (tbox v2.7.0). Ratified from a real cross-session proposal (a registrant package's own RegisterPackageShape/Role_ProgressReport requirement had no matching naming convention); checked directly against the existing sibling before building, not assumed from the proposal's own description."@en,
        "v2.8.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): every named subject now carries dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/configuration> (its module), the first step of the consolidation of this package's files into one file per role. No term, label or definition changed."@en ;
